          "explanation": "The popular flattened version strips out Marx's genuine sympathy: he explicitly calls religion 'the sigh of the oppressed creature' and 'the heart of a heartless world,' acknowledging it expresses real suffering, before going on to critique its anesthetic, hope-redirecting function. His stated target is the oppressive material conditions requiring such consolation in the first place.",
