          "explanation": "The Young Hegelians shared Hegel's dialectical, critical method (not a total break from Hegel) but applied it subversively — against the established church and the Prussian state Hegel's own late work had tended to defend. Feuerbach, Bauer, Stirner, and the young Marx and Engels disagreed substantively with one another, which is why understanding them as a loose critical movement, not a unified doctrine, matters.",
